JSON helpers: schema.to_dict/from_dict (report_type-routed via SCHEMA_BY_TYPE), to_json/from_json. Round-trip verified lossless for all 19 docs (test_every_document_round_trips_through_json).

EXTRACTOR (src/sars/extract_data.py): extract_report(doc, name) classifies tables on demand, builds ReportMeta from banner text lines + catalogue, routes to a per-family extractor (school_result_slip/best_students/schools_rank/top_schools/subjects_rank) or the generic header-driven fallback. Column->field mapping is header-driven: _column_headers() flattens the multi-row header band across colspans/rowspans into per-column label paths (e.g. 'DIVISION PERFORMANCE / I / F'); _fmt_groups() groups F/M/T/% under their parent segment; row_kinds skip banner/header/total CHROME rows; total-row DATA kept in .totals keyed by the (chrome) label. School slip handles candidate tables that split across pages (continuation tables have no header + a leading blank column) by locating the CNO id column and the SEX column dynamically, capturing all 380 candidates, and also captures the registration/subject-performance/grade summary tables into slip.performance.

CLI: `sars data [--only NAME]` (cli.cmd_data) writes output/data/<name>.json for each doc (prints JSON when --only). All 19 JSON files emitted to output/data/. NOTE for orchestrator: output/data/ is covered by .gitignore (like output/html|pdf|compare which are force-committed); the 19 JSON files must be added with `git add -f 'output/data/*.json'` to be committed, matching how the other output artefacts are tracked.

GAPS/NOTES: subject_school_rank, wards_rank, district_performance, mock_mobility use GenericTabularReport (lossless header-keyed capture) rather than bespoke typed schemas - fully extracted, just not strongly typed, per the plan's guidance to prioritise the main families. FEAT-004 (templates/rendering, name-by-level, colour discrepancy fixes) and FEAT-005 (deeper assertions) are out of scope for this feature.
